//! The `font-width` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property selects a
//! normal, condensed, or expanded face from a font.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - condensed: Specifies a more condensed font face than normal, with `ultra-condensed` being the
//! most condensed.
//! - expanded: Specifies a more expanded font face than normal, with `ultra-expanded` being the most
//! expanded.
//! - extra-condensed: Specifies a more condensed font face than normal, with `ultra-condensed` being
//! the most condensed.
//! - extra-expanded: Specifies a more expanded font face than normal, with `ultra-expanded` being
//! the most expanded.
//! - normal: Specifies a normally condensed font face.
//! - semi-condensed: Specifies a more condensed font face than normal, with `ultra-condensed` being
//! the most condensed.
//! - semi-expanded: Specifies a more expanded font face than normal, with `ultra-expanded` being the
//! most expanded.
//! - ultra-condensed: Specifies a more condensed font face than normal, with `ultra-condensed` being
//! the most condensed.
//! - ultra-expanded: Specifies a more expanded font face than normal, with `ultra-expanded` being
//! the most expanded.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | <percentage [0,∞]> | ultra-condensed | extra-condensed | condensed |
//! semi-condensed | semi-expanded | expanded | extra-expanded | ultra-expanded
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#propdef-font-width
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-width
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

